{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJW9zajmzJDxRjEqCE36","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've solved it, written the full proof to `/work/answer.md`, and created `/work/SUBMIT`, which ends the attempt.\n\n**Answer:** a stable set exists exactly when K is even. For K = 2h there is only one: {(h,h,0), (h,0,h), (0,h,h)}. For odd K there are none. The continuum's discriminatory solutions have no grid version: an allocation where player 3 gets one unit more than the fixed share can only be beaten by making both other players better off, which needs two extra units, and only one is available.\n\n**How the proof goes:**\n- **Pairs inside a stable set:** if neither of two allocations in the set beats the other, each must be ahead in exactly one coordinate. So any two members share exactly one coordinate value.\n- **What that forces:** the set either lies entirely on one line where some player's share is fixed, or it is exactly three points of the form T − d·e_i, one for each player i.\n- **Ruling things out:** in every case except T = (d,d,d) with K = 2d, I name an allocation outside the set that nothing in the set beats. That makes every other set fail, and leaves only the symmetric set, which needs K even.\n- **Checking it works:** I also show directly that the symmetric set is stable whenever K is even.\n\n**Computer checks:** an exhaustive search (`/work/code/enum.py`) found exactly this result for every K from 2 to 14. The provided `check.py` also confirms the symmetric set is stable for K = 2, 4, 6 and 10."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3393,"cache_read_input_tokens":26338,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3393,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"30f00570-dc25-46e3-9c52-20e44ad13426","uuid":"abe7683e-f22c-4e50-9905-f7b09d8e394e","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:02:25.762Z","request_id":"req_011CgJW9zF98k5GPH9aKP46w"}
