 in the set beats the other, each must be ahead in exactly one coordinate. So any two members share exactly one coordinate value.\n- **What that forces:** the set either lies entirely on one line where some player's share is fixed, or it is exactly three points of the form T − d·e_i, one for each player i.\n- **Ruling things out:** in every case except T = (d,d,d) with K = 2d, I name an allocation outside the set that nothing in the set beats. That makes every other set fail, and leaves only the symmetric set, which needs K even.\n- **Checking it works:** I also show directly that the symmetric set is stable whenever K is even.\n\n**Computer checks:** an exhaustive search (`/work/code/enum.py`) found exactly this result for every K from 2 to 14. The provided `check.py` also confirms the symmetric set is stable for K = 2, 4, 6 and 10.","ttft_ms":2174,"type":"result","duration_ms":129724,"uuid":"ade0ed78-180e-4e45-b7ef-46dc9fcf6e3a","ttft_stream_ms":1900,"time_to_request_ms":94,"first_content_frame_ms":1901,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":14,"outputTokens":11723,"cacheReadInputTokens":126356,"cacheCreationInputTokens":18644,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3530072,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":6868,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
